   <p>To His Excellency
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N001000">Thos E Bramblett</persName>
<lb/>Governor of <orgName ref="cwgk:O001025">Kentucky</orgName></p>
<p>Your petitioner would respectfully represent that at the <date>March Term of the <orgName ref="cwgk:O00000358">Bath Circuit Court</orgName> 1861</date> there was a Judgement rendered in behalf of the Commonwealth for twenty dollars against <persName ref="cwgk:N00018663">James Wells Jr</persName>- That James Wells Jr is now a private in <persName ref="cwgk:N00018662">Cap L. North's</persName> Comp<hi rend="sup">y</hi> of the <orgName ref="cwgk:O00006977">24<hi rend="sup">th</hi> Regt Kentucky Vol Infantry</orgName> &amp; on duty in the ranks at or near <placeName ref="cwgk:P00005704">Knoxville</placeName> <placeName ref="cwgk:P001001">Tenn</placeName> That an execution has lately been issued on said Judgt and has been levied on said James Well<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">s</hi></hi> property</p>
<p>Your petitioner would earnestly pray your Excellency to remit said fine</p>
<p><date when="1864-02-12">Feb 12<hi rend="sup">th</hi> 1864</date></p>
<p><milestone unit="column" n="2"/><cb n="2"/><persName ref="cwgk:N00000476">B D Lacy</persName>
